{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"The Warding Tree: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja71'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 71 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Varuṇavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Warding Tree </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>1. Varuṇajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Warding Tree: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Yo pubbe karaṇīyāni, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Whoever wishes to do afterwards </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>pacchā so kātumicchati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>tasks they should have done before, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Varuṇakaṭṭhabhañjova, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>like the one who broke a branch off the Warding Tree, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sa pacchā manutappatī”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>afterwards is tormented by regrets. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Varuṇajātakaṁ paṭhamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
